{
  "schema": "open77.vehicle-kit.plates/1",
  "summary": "Production plate pack, route W, for the 15 Light RP dealer models, the staff-only Rayfield Caliburn and every other vanilla player vehicle (Vehicle.*_player*, cars and motorcycles, except the quest variants Vehicle.q<digits>_* left out by the owner on 2026-11-07: the models with a `generated` field, written by player-models.py from the player inventory). One ArchiveXL .app patch per vanilla appearance resource adds our own components, by definition name, to every definition that has (or can carry) a rear plate: a screen quad over the plate and a WorldWidgetComponent that draws an .inkwidget on it. The components are disabled by default, so traffic and unowned cars look factory; the client enables them when the server sets a plate text (client/redscript/Open77VehiclePlate.reds). No vanilla definition, component or file is copied: vanilla resources are referenced by depot path only.",  "resource": "open77_vehicle_plates",
  "archiveName": "open77_vehicle_plates",
  "componentNames": {
    "screen": "open77_plate_screen",
    "text": "open77_plate_text",
    "mount": "open77_plate_mount",
    "frontSuffix": "_f",
    "note": "The REDscript finds these exact names. Changing one is a client contract change."
  },
  "screenMesh": {
    "path": "base\\environment\\decoration\\electronics\\entertainment\\television\\television_neokitsch_21x9_screen_a.mesh",
    "appearance": "interactive_screen",
    "material": "base\\materials\\screen\\screen_ui.mi",
    "note": "4-vertex two-sided quad in its XZ plane, measured by sub-agent H and re-checked by this build: its UVs read correctly from +Y (u grows towards -X). Placement maps that reading frame onto the plate's holo layer."
  },
  "plateMeshes": {
    "base\\vehicles\\common\\parts\\v_common_licenseplate\\entities\\meshes\\license_plate.mesh": { "holoChunk": 1, "item": "Car", "style": "car", "legacyAspect": 3.3, "note": "cars; a top bar plus a flat holo layer hanging below it" },
    "base\\vehicles\\common\\parts\\v_common_licenseplate\\entities\\meshes\\license_plate_small.mesh": { "holoChunk": 3, "item": "Moto", "style": "bike", "legacyAspect": 1.11, "note": "bikes (Apollo basic, Kusanagi)" },
    "base\\vehicles\\common\\parts\\v_common_licenseplate\\entities\\meshes\\license_plate_angle_01.mesh": { "holoChunk": 3, "item": "MotoTilt", "style": "bike", "legacyAspect": 1.11, "note": "Apollo police and player_02; the holo layer is bent, the quad lies on its chord (the plane of least depth spread, 4.6 mm)" },
    "base\\vehicles\\common\\parts\\v_common_licenseplate\\entities\\meshes\\motorcycle_license_plate.mesh": { "holoChunk": 1, "item": "MotoWide", "style": "bike", "legacyAspect": 1.11, "note": "Kusanagi player_02 / player_03; a frame around the holo" }
  },
  "plateMeshesNote": "item: the library item of the design drawn on that mesh, authored at the aspect of its quad; style: the design proportions and region label (inkwidget.cjs STYLES); legacyAspect: the design aspect the superseded fit rule used on that mesh, kept only to measure the defect it left (before/after table).",
  "placement": {
    "rule": "cover",
    "proudMetres": 0.003,
    "coverMaxViewDegrees": 60,
    "coverExtraMetres": 0.001,
    "clearanceMetres": 0.0015,
    "parallelDegrees": 25,
    "mountHidesHolo": true,
    "leakStepMetres": 0.002,
    "leakAzimuths": 24,
    "leakConeDegrees": [10, 20, 30, 40, 50, 60],
    "leakSideDegrees": [0, 30, 45, 60, 70, 80],
    "legacyMarginMetres": 0.015,
    "mountGapMetres": 0.002,
    "mountMaxShiftMetres": 0.25,
    "mountMinHits": 6,
    "note": "Cover rule (native/cover.cjs). The quad lies proudMetres in front of the holo layer's outermost point; a visible plate surface within clearanceMetres of that plane and within parallelDegrees of parallel to it pushes the quad out in front of it. The quad covers the holo rectangle grown on every side by gap * tan(coverMaxViewDegrees) + coverExtraMetres, gap being the distance from the quad to the deepest holo point, so no ray leaving the holo within coverMaxViewDegrees of the plate normal can miss it. The build casts those rays (leak*: one sample per leakStepMetres squared, leakAzimuths azimuths per cone angle) and fails on any print seen. mountHidesHolo: a mounted plate, which is ours, is authored with its holo chunk masked out of chunkMask, as vanilla hides whole plates on burnt definitions (chunkMask 0). legacyMarginMetres: the superseded fit rule (quad inside the holo at legacyAspect, proudMetres in front of every vertex over the holo grown by this margin), measured for the before/after table only. Mounts: a definition without a rear plate gets the vanilla plate mesh, by depot path, when a sibling definition of the same .app has a rear plate on the same slot: the sibling's placement is cast onto this definition's rear bumper mesh along the plate normal, and the plate goes mountGapMetres in front of the rearmost hit."
  },
  "excludeDefinitions": "burnt|destroyed|damage|no_wheels",
  "front": true,
  "designs": {
    "original": {
      "generated": "open77_plate.inkwidget",
      "textPath": "PlateText",
      "fonts": {
        "text": { "family": "base\\gameplay\\gui\\fonts\\orbitron\\orbitron.inkfontfamily", "style": "Bold", "license": "Orbitron, SIL Open Font License 1.1" },
        "region": { "family": "base\\gameplay\\gui\\fonts\\raj\\raj.inkfontfamily", "style": "Bold", "license": "Rajdhani, SIL Open Font License 1.1" }
      },
      "colors": {
        "background": [0.035, 0.043, 0.071, 1],
        "border": [0.37, 0.96, 1.0, 1],
        "band": [0.98, 0.93, 0.0, 1],
        "region": [0.035, 0.043, 0.071, 1],
        "text": [0.93, 0.98, 1.0, 1]
      },
      "regionLabel": { "car": "NIGHT CITY", "bike": "NC" },
      "note": "Our own design: a library with one item per plate mesh (plateMeshes item), each authored at the aspect of that mesh's quad: the design inside the holo rectangle, the margin in the background colour, nothing stretched. Only rectangles and two texts, no logic controller, the game's OFL fonts by depot path. The region label and colours are placeholders for the owner."
    }
  },
  "retiredDesigns": {
    "sign": { "widget": "base\\gameplay\\gui\\world\\street_signs\\generic_street_name\\generic_street_name_sign.inkwidget", "textPath": "StreetNameContainer/StreetName", "aspect": 3.3, "why": "A vanilla widget has one fixed aspect and cannot be letterboxed. The cover quads are 2.49 (car) down to 1.09 (small bike plate), so the sign would be stretched 1.3x to 3x; an opaque backing quad would need a component the client does not toggle (client contract change). Proved route W in game (E0.7, Galena); superseded by original." },
    "lcd": { "widget": "base\\gameplay\\gui\\world\\street_signs\\generic_screens\\lcdscreen_10x1.inkwidget", "textPath": "default_ui/messege_text", "aspect": 10.0, "why": "Same as sign, at aspect 10. Never measured in game." }
  },
  "variants": {
    "disabled": { "screen": false, "text": false, "mount": false, "note": "the only variant: every added component is authored disabled; the client enables them when a text is set. An 'enabled widget' variant would buy nothing: vanilla VehicleObject.OnGameAttached disables every UI widget of the car at each spawn anyway (SetInteriorUIEnabled(false)), and a disabled widget toggled on spawns and renders at once (measured in game, 2026-11-05)." }
  },
